---
title: "is_admin (kintai-v3: Initial Schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_uid: uid = auth.uid()
    q_get_uid --> q_lookup: SELECT role FROM users WHERE id = uid
    q_lookup --> q_check_role: row found
    q_lookup --> q_coalesce: row not found
    q_coalesce --> q_return_false: coalesce(NULL, 0) = 0, return false
    q_check_role --> q_return_true: role = 1
    q_check_role --> q_return_false: role != 1
    q_return_true --> [*]: return true
    q_return_false --> [*]: return false

    note right of q_get_uid
        INV-001: auth.uid() returns the JWT-authenticated user ID from Supabase Auth
        INV-002: Function is SECURITY DEFINER - executes with owner privileges
        INV-003: search_path is set to public to prevent schema injection
    end note

    note right of q_lookup
        INV-004: If user has no row in public.users, coalesce defaults to 0 (non-admin)
        INV-005: role integer values - 0 = member, 1 = admin
    end note
